  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>To get snacks for a class trip, Clare went to the “bulk” section of the grocery store, where she could buy any quantity of a product and the prices are usually good.</para>
<para>Clare purchased some salted almonds at $6 a pound and some dried figs at $9 per pound. She spent $75 before tax.</para>
<div><figure><media alt="Bowl of figs and almonds."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5b214f5db89f6f9b4cdc2315a7a917f873009470"/></media></figure></div>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="5fc6775e-5c6d-4b5d-b1a2-a0cd96ac38f6" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="58b7491f-9daa-42f2-808a-e8da96a4cf85" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="7">
    <problem>
      <para>If she bought 2 pounds of almonds, how many pounds of figs did she buy?
        </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 7</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7bbc8bae-d928-47af-a361-13d9354c1358" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="11">
    <problem>
      <para>If she bought 1 pound of figs, how many pounds of almonds did she buy?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 11</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>

<!--Q3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Write an <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="storename">equation</term> that describes the relationship between pounds of figs and pounds of almonds that Clare bought and the dollar amount that she paid. Be sure to specify what the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="storename">variables</term> represent.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(6a+9f=75\)
      \(a\): pounds of almonds, \(f\): pounds of figs</para>
    <para>For questions 4 and 5, use the graph that represents the quantities in the situation.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<para>For questions 4 and 5, use the graph that represents the quantities in the situation.
</para>
<figure><media alt="Graph of 2 intersecting lines and 5 points, origin O, with grid. Almonds (pounds) and dried figs (pounds)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6228bf48d50ee3aeb03d98c3cff3716dedb54f41"/></media></figure><!--Q4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Choose any point on the line, state its coordinates, and explain what it tells us.
      </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
      Point A or (2, 7). Clare bought 2 pounds of almonds and 7 pounds of figs for a total of $75.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Q5-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Choose any point that is not on the line, state its coordinates, and explain what it tells us.
      </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
      Point D or \((1, 1)\). Clare bought 1 pound of almonds and 1 pound of figs, and the total was not $75.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


